            "review_title": "Review at King Poutine",
            "review_text": "Jocelyngravel\n86 contributions\n0\nThe best poutine in eastern Canada\nMar 2026 • Couples\nKing poutine is a restaurant honouring a distinctly Canadian delicacy (it originates in the province of Quebec), poutine. After living and working as a chef for several years in Canada, Chef Rang returned to his homeland of Vietnam to open the first poutine restaurant in the country. The quality of the food is at the level. \n\nThe poutine is excellent, the sauce is homemade and it is one of the good poutine sauces I have eaten in my life. Believe me, I ate poutines as a 55-year-old Quebecer. French fries are OK because there is no potato in Vietnam. So we have to import the fries from New Zealand. Unlike many international restaurants, Chef Rang uses quality grain cheese imported from Canada. It's not the best cheese in grain, but it's OK. This is the hardest thing for a poutine outside of Quebec. \n\nThe service is very friendly and fast.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from French\nShow original\nWritten March 24, 2026",
